rake_keyword — Rapid Automatic Keyword Extraction
=================================================

Source:   https://github.com/u-prashant/RAKE  (package `rake`, MIT)
Author:   Prashant Upadhyay
License:  MIT (see LICENSE in this directory)

Why it is here
--------------
Nighthawk reads a query before it fetches anything: which phrase is the
subject, which words are filler, what kind of thing the person wants. RAKE is
the keyword/phrase half of that — it scores candidate phrases from word degree
and frequency without a model file, a download, or a network call, which is the
only kind of thing that can run on a free instance with no data directory.

What was changed
----------------
Nothing in rake.py. The file is vendored verbatim so it can be read against
upstream. The default stop-word path (`resources/SmartStoplist.txt`, relative to
the process working directory) is supplied explicitly by
`apps/api/app/understand.py`, which points at the copy shipped here.

SmartStoplist.txt is the Fox/Smart stop list that ships with RAKE upstream
(originally from https://github.com/aneesha/RAKE, MIT).
